24903:
One photon carries E = \frac{h c}{\lambda} = \frac{6.63 \times 10^{-34} \times 3 \times 10^8}{663 \times 10^{-9}} = 3.0 \times 10^{-19} \text{ J}
Emission rate n = \frac{P}{E} = \frac{6.0 \times 10^{-3}}{3.0 \times 10^{-19}} = 2.0 \times 10^{16} \text{ s}^{-1}
Hence 2 \times 10^{16} photons per second → (A)

24906:
