With propagation along +\hat{k} and \vec{E} along \hat{j}, the relation \hat{j} \times (-\hat{i}) = \hat{k} forces \vec{B} along -\hat{i}
\vec{B} = -1.8 \times 10^{-7} \sin(k z - \omega t) \hat{i} \text{ T} → (A)

24909:
Mean free path \lambda = \frac{k_B T}{\sqrt{2} \pi d^2 P}
\lambda = \frac{1.38 \times 10^{-23} \times 314}{1.414 \times 3.14 \times (5 \times 10^{-10})^2 \times 1.38 \times 10^5} \approx 2.8 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m}
The mean free path is 2.8 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m} → (A)

24910:
With the Cartesian sign convention u = -30 \text{ cm} and f = +20 \text{ cm}
\frac{1}{v} = \frac{1}{f} + \frac{1}{u} = \frac{1}{20} - \frac{1}{30} = \frac{1}{60}, so v = +60 \text{ cm}
m = \frac{v}{u} = \frac{60}{-30} = -2, a real inverted image → (A)

24911:
On the frictionless plane the masses oscillate about the centre of mass with reduced mass \mu = \frac{1 \times 0.2}{1 + 0.2} = \frac{1}{6} \text{ kg}
\omega = \sqrt{\frac{k}{\mu}} = \sqrt{\frac{150}{1 / 6}} = \sqrt{900} = 30 \text{ rad/s}
The angular frequency is 30 rad/s → (A)

24914:
The slide length is s = \frac{L}{\cos \theta}, and in the incline frame a pseudo force adds a_0 \cos \theta down the slope to g \sin \theta
s = \frac{1}{2} a_{\text{eff}} t^2 gives t = \sqrt{\frac{2 L}{\cos \theta (g \sin \theta + a_0 \cos \theta)}}
With \sin 2\theta = 2 \sin \theta \cos \theta and 1 + \cos 2\theta = 2 \cos^2 \theta this becomes \sqrt{\frac{4 L}{g \sin 2\theta + a_0 (1 + \cos 2\theta)}} → (A)

24915:
v = \sqrt{\frac{Y}{\rho}} gives \frac{\Delta v}{v} = \frac{1}{2} \frac{\Delta Y}{Y} - \frac{1}{2} \frac{\Delta \rho}{\rho}
\frac{\Delta v}{v} = \frac{1}{2} \times 1.0\% - \frac{1}{2} \times 0.5\% = +0.25\%
New speed 400 \times 1.0025 = 401 \text{ m/s} → (D)

24917:
Inside the conductor Ampere's law encloses only part of the current, giving B = \frac{\mu_0 I r}{2 \pi R^2}
B = 0 at the axis r = 0 and grows linearly to its maximum at the surface r = R
Zero at the axis and maximum at the surface → (A)

